WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.500
Hey, welcome to 40 Days of Holiness. I'm Darrell Stetler.

2
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.340
I'm really thankful you're here, and I can't wait to teach you some of the things

3
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.660
that the scripture has taught me about God and His holiness.

4
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.390
Holiness is a mega theme of scripture, and we're going to see how incredibly

5
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.420
meaningful this concept is and how it changes our view of God and

6
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.460
ourselves. Now, I want to encourage you to make sure and download

7
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.420
the 40-day guide, the workbook that's included with this course.

8
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.400
Don't just watch and listen. I want you

9
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.400
instead to also write. The reason that's important is because

10
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.720
it'll help you process and think through what the scripture's saying,

11
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.020
and most importantly, just help you put it into practice.

12
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.200
Because it's not just what you read, it's what you do of the Bible.

13
00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.630
Here's what I'm going to imagine for this 40 days.

14
00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.280
I'm going to imagine that you came to me and you said, "Darrell,

15
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.700
I really want to be a holy man, a holy woman.

16
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.320
I want to grow in holiness.

17
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.900
And I was wondering, Darrell, if you would meet with me for 40 days and just teach

18
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.760
me in bite-sized chunks what the scripture says about being

19
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:17.780
as holy, as much like Jesus in my heart and my life

20
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.360
as God can possibly make me." And I'm going to imagine that I said yes.

21
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:25.260
And so here we are. We are gathered together in a coffee shop.

22
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.190
I've got my iced coffee right here.

23
00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.970
And I'm going to imagine that we've both sat down across the

24
00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.800
table, and we're going to spend five to 10 minutes each day just talking

25
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.840
about holiness and what the scripture says.

26
00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.480
I'm going to send you home with homework. That's the workbook.

27
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.480
Sample prayers, meditation questions, and stuff like that.

28
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.580
And just trust that the Holy Spirit is going to do powerful work in

29
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.930
you all through this 40 days.

30
00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.970
Now, today's day one. So grab your workbook and let's get started.

31
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.520
From time to time, I'll scribble on my

32
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.640
coffee shop napkin over here. If you want to know about holiness, we have to start

33
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.500
with God. Day one, God is holy and the source

34
00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:07.560
of all holiness. In Isaiah 6:3, we read, "Holy, holy,

35
00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.320
holy is the Lord Almighty. The whole earth is full of His

36
00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.060
glory." And in Revelation 4:8, we read another picture of the worship in

37
00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:19.049
heaven where it says, "Day and night, they never stop saying: Holy,

38
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.240
holy, holy is the Lord God Almighty, who was,

39
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.450
and is, and is to come."

40
00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:30.240
Now, it's appropriate that we take a moment and we recognize that

41
00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.880
all holiness is built on the reality and sourced

42
00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.860
from God. God is at His core and in His essence,

43
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.920
holy love. And in Heaven, these scenes from the scripture

44
00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.520
teach us that special creations like angels call out,

45
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.440
"Holy, holy, holy," continually.

46
00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.680
Now, that Trinitarian repetition of holy is significant

47
00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:55.340
because it's three in one, but also because it's the only thing repeated

48
00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.020
around God's throne in that way. He is faithful, yes, He is

49
00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.670
powerful, He's knowledgeable, but in His essence, He is

50
00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.660
holy. So what is that? Well, He's separate.

51
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.620
He's other. He's not like. He's untouched by the

52
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.700
faults and weakness and dependence of all other things.

53
00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.100
He is completely other than His creation.

54
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.850
There's only two things in all of existence, God and creation, God and

55
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.300
everything else. And that utter, unique, separate

56
00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.240
purity is His holiness. Now, out of

57
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.760
this flow all of His other attributes.

58
00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:34.860
Everything else is eventually unfaithful, but God is faithfulness

59
00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.840
unmixed. Everything else is dependent and needy, but

60
00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.700
God is completely independent, unneedy.

61
00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.980
Everything else has a spot of corruption, but God is

62
00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.480
unmixed purity.

63
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.160
Everything else has its light and its darkness, its yin and its yang, but

64
00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.780
God is completely unmixed, completely single and whole,

65
00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.630
utterly alone in His degree of perfection.

66
00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:04.760
Now, this holiness in scripture is often expressed as

67
00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.380
incomprehensible, blinding, terrifying light or

68
00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.230
purifying fire. To be in the presence of God's complete holiness

69
00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.300
would literally kill your physical body, as if you'd been suddenly transported

70
00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.750
to within 100 miles of the sun. You couldn't physically or

71
00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.960
spiritually take the glory of His holiness.

72
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.270
Now, I don't mean to suggest that God's holiness is a negative thing as though it

73
00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.560
was a source of pain or fear.

74
00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:34.400
On the contrary, God's holiness is so glorious, so

75
00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:38.480
joyful, so explosively brilliant that its beauty

76
00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.790
and goodness is what's overwhelming.

77
00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:45.380
The Bible tells us to worship the Lord in the beauty of holiness, not the horror

78
00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:49.390
or fear of holiness. But people have often noticed that for us as

79
00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.430
humans, there's this place where joy gets so overwhelming that

80
00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.130
it gets close to something like terror.

81
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.900
Like the sheer terror as you're about to descend the world's tallest,

82
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.140
fastest roller coaster. Your stomach knots up and leaps up in

83
00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:07.820
your throat. You can't speak, your breath is gone, and the

84
00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.840
joy and the terror for a few moments just overwhelms you.

85
00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.440
Now, even if you don't like roller coasters, you know what I mean.

86
00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:19.980
Recently, I joined my teenage son, and we jumped off

87
00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.400
the top of a bridge that was over a lake.

88
00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.200
We climbed the top, and we walked the beams along the top, and we

89
00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.980
looked down at the lake 25 feet below, and it was higher from up

90
00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.960
there than it was from down below. And then we jumped.

91
00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.520
And the rush, the adrenaline, the feeling of, "I think I must be crazy."

92
00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.350
Now, maybe you're not a jump off a bridge kind of person,

93
00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.460
but the point still stands.

94
00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.300
The joy and the terror meet somewhere in

95
00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:53.000
there. And in the same way, the joyous

96
00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:57.190
terror of God's holiness would simply overwhelm you in every

97
00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.860
way, physically, mentally, emotionally, spiritually.

98
00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.060
It's not that it's so bad that it's scary.

99
00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:07.120
It's that it's so good, it's marvelously overwhelming.

100
00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.220
So where does God get His holiness?

101
00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.640
Well, God's holiness doesn't come from anywhere.

102
00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.870
It is underived. It isn't received from anything or

103
00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.920
anywhere. Instead, God is the fountainhead, the source,

104
00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.720
the definition of holiness. Biblically, the word

105
00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:28.700
holy only means someone who is rightly related to

106
00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.780
God in some way.

107
00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.340
Any holiness in the world

108
00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.520
came from God. Any holiness in an item or a

109
00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.600
place came from God. Any holiness in a person, you can be

110
00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:44.420
sure it came from God. And if you achieve any

111
00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.940
holiness in your life, you can be sure you didn't create it.

112
00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.340
It came from God. So God is holy. He's the source

113
00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:56.300
of all holiness. And today, starting today, we're going to spend 40

114
00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:59.600
days journeying deep into that holiness,

115
00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.800
chasing the beauty and joy of His holiness and letting that

116
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:07.040
holiness seep down into us.

117
00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.130
So I'm looking forward to it. Thanks for being here.

118
00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:14.280
Take your workbook and spend the time to do the sample prayer,

119
00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:18.340
think over the meditation questions, and be just continuing on in

120
00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.300
your growth and your desire to think through these things.

121
00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:25.140
And let the Holy Spirit work that work in you

122
00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.860
as you're going through this 40 days. I'm looking forward to it.

123
00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:30.360
Thanks for taking the time to be here today. See you tomorrow.
